WEBVTT

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:02.320
Thank you.

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:47.900
I know where he is.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:48.120
I know where he is.

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:48.360
You do?

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:50.890
With your permission.

00:02:06.190 --> 00:02:07.090
There he is now!

00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:11.190
Oh, am I glad to see you!

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:13.900
What are you doing here with Chi-Chek?

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:16.680
The dragons are going to bomb the airport and aim to fly to Scotland.

00:02:17.050 --> 00:02:18.470
Chi-Chek came here to revenge you.

00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:20.440
Oh, Madala? Bomb the airport?

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:23.580
If I can get to the dragon's hat out on time, I'll stop him.

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:25.280
But the dragons have been armed to fight out.

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:26.440
They're on their way to the airport.

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:28.060
Well, why, that's perfect.

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:29.970
And the dragon's death ray on his door...

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:32.160
There'll be no one there to stop you.

00:02:32.570 --> 00:02:34.250
If I can get away from these fellows.

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:35.850
The only one has much influence.

00:02:36.070 --> 00:02:36.930
You're afraid to go now.

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:37.610
Oh, well.

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:40.700
You can drive me tough for a couple minutes.

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:42.160
I've got to borrow a car in a hurry.

00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:03.850
Meriden.

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:05.700
We drove off the dragon way.

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:07.580
No, just when we're prepared for another attack,

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:09.140
they suddenly fell out of control and crashed.

00:05:09.590 --> 00:05:10.350
Fire squadron.

00:05:16.180 --> 00:05:17.740
It's the Dragon plane. I'm going after him.

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:19.950
No, I don't think so.

00:05:20.190 --> 00:05:22.050
A pursuit plane, a number three hangar ought to be okay.

00:05:25.140 --> 00:05:26.820
Pull that chip out as fast as you can, boys.

00:05:26.980 --> 00:05:27.800
I'm taking off in a hurry.

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:28.890
Okay.

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:34.360
You

00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:04.690
Don't come in today.

00:06:06.010 --> 00:06:06.990
There's something you ought to know.

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:07.510
What is it?

00:06:07.930 --> 00:06:09.450
Still stick for the dragon slaves attack.

00:06:09.670 --> 00:06:11.350
Winston left the airport under circumstances.

00:06:11.730 --> 00:06:12.690
which makes me believe

00:06:12.950 --> 00:06:14.250
he knew what was going to happen

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:15.420
Winston, what do you mean?

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:17.320
He went out of his way to take a fall.

00:06:17.720 --> 00:06:19.220
because of your handling, it's very good.

00:06:19.700 --> 00:06:21.060
You mean, you think Winston is a dragon?

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:22.000
Yes, I do.

00:06:22.330 --> 00:06:23.210
Oh, that ain't...

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:25.420
Find out if you're right, Meredith.

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:32.720
Second final.

00:06:58.850 --> 00:06:59.930
and drop down.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:00.500
by plane.

00:07:01.340 --> 00:07:01.920
The dragon!

00:07:04.630 --> 00:07:05.270
Well, well.

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:07.900
We didn't know it was Boogeyman himself.

00:07:08.410 --> 00:07:09.710
You'll do well to smile.

00:07:10.460 --> 00:07:11.900
We have a saying in Mongolia.

00:07:12.760 --> 00:07:15.180
He who smiles at the grave's head.

00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:17.910
Take happiness into the world beyond.

00:07:19.610 --> 00:07:21.510
It's got a saying in America, too, you know.

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:24.310
Don't count your chickens before they're hacked.

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:26.580
You'll never leave this place alive.

00:07:28.120 --> 00:07:28.440
Thank you very much.

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:29.620
You rubbed me out.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:32.320
Just give an aide someone one more reason to kiss you.

00:07:33.100 --> 00:07:37.820
It may interest you to know that I shot Drummond down at the airport during the attack.

00:07:53.420 --> 00:07:54.120
He didn't kill him!

00:07:54.730 --> 00:07:55.690
He won't get away.

00:07:56.390 --> 00:07:57.370
Thank you.

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:01.540
Don't try to warn him.

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:42.020
We heard it at all.

00:08:43.590 --> 00:08:43.990
Thank you.

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:45.880
You're getting away from that tunnel, ladies.

00:08:46.700 --> 00:08:47.120
Oh, we got him.

00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:56.620
All right.

00:08:58.660 --> 00:08:59.900
Half of the mountain falls.

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:02.280
The dragon must have had this passing line.

00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:05.200
But the look of the things, he had that outside entrance block, too.

00:09:05.710 --> 00:09:07.350
Boy, that guy never misses a death.

00:09:08.460 --> 00:09:10.580
We're gonna be in here for a long, long time.

00:09:11.490 --> 00:09:12.430
We've got to get out of here, Jerry,

00:09:12.530 --> 00:09:14.130
before the dragon gets hold of Peggy and her father.

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:19.530
A runner has just arrived from the village,

00:09:19.630 --> 00:09:22.090
saying the dragon's train has been shot down at the airport.

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:24.040
He must have got the other time.

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:26.420
The dragon's power is broken at last.

00:09:27.010 --> 00:09:29.030
Danny, I'm so glad, now you'll be safe.

00:09:29.250 --> 00:09:29.970
You won't have to keep...

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:32.240
I'll take you straight, not my secret, any longer.

00:09:32.680 --> 00:09:35.000
That secret has cost too many lives already.

00:09:35.660 --> 00:09:38.620
I'm going to keep it until Ace Drummond tells me the dragon is done.

00:09:39.270 --> 00:09:40.070
I think...

00:09:40.330 --> 00:09:42.030
You are very wise, my friend.

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:44.680
It's the hour of the evening parable, isn't it?

00:09:45.420 --> 00:09:45.460
Thank you.

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:45.940
All right.

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:49.120
We must leave you now.

00:09:50.920 --> 00:09:51.220
Amen.

00:09:52.140 --> 00:09:52.480
Thank you.

00:09:54.220 --> 00:09:57.940
If you open the window and want the discussion back, that's what I feel, it would be good.

00:10:25.750 --> 00:10:27.190
Evening air is chill, holy one.

00:10:27.410 --> 00:10:28.510
I will fetch you a cake.

00:10:31.500 --> 00:10:32.480
Thank you.

00:10:36.260 --> 00:10:37.940
Dad, just look up archaeology, Dad.

00:10:38.310 --> 00:10:39.670
You look adorable, huh?

00:10:57.100 --> 00:10:58.400
I'm going away from the apartment, Mr. Hayden.

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:02.390
Don't make it sound either.

00:11:05.720 --> 00:11:06.560
You're guarding the beam.

00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:09.740
I promise.

00:11:16.600 --> 00:11:16.940
Dragon.

00:11:17.530 --> 00:11:18.350
Take off that helmet.

00:11:21.620 --> 00:11:23.180
You heard me? Take off that helmet.

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:28.220
Good work, blummin'.

00:11:30.600 --> 00:11:34.100
Mr. Drummond, how on earth did you get here?

00:11:34.380 --> 00:11:35.600
Where is Dr. Traynor?

00:11:36.150 --> 00:11:37.110
In his room, holy one.

00:11:39.360 --> 00:11:40.280
Take off that helmet.

00:11:47.450 --> 00:11:50.450
You whom I cherish above all I respect,

00:11:56.070 --> 00:11:58.330
vows you have taken part of my life.

00:12:00.220 --> 00:12:01.820
You are a distraught, Walter.

00:12:02.810 --> 00:12:04.350
He isn't one of your people, Holy One.

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:07.700
The credentials he brought from the Grand Lama at Lassa are forged.

00:12:08.680 --> 00:12:11.020
He is a white man, born and raised among your people.

00:12:11.640 --> 00:12:14.480
The language and customs he learned as his own.

00:12:15.180 --> 00:12:17.520
Why have you done this evil thing?

00:12:18.010 --> 00:12:19.430
What did you hope to be?

00:12:20.620 --> 00:12:23.070
If it hadn't been for common interference,

00:12:23.090 --> 00:12:26.010
I would have made myself the most powerful man in age.

00:12:27.010 --> 00:12:29.970
You dare to use our religion as a cloak for you?

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:41.220
your selfishness, names of Holy One, whose temple you have outfitted, destroyed.

00:12:44.930 --> 00:12:51.160
Send the guards to head him off.

00:14:04.890 --> 00:14:07.650
It's no use, my friend. If they can't catch them, you can't eat it.

00:14:44.430 --> 00:14:45.590
They go off the wind, but he's back.

00:14:46.480 --> 00:14:47.280
He'll never clear the monastery.

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:16.340
Thanks to you, Drummond, International Airways has now accomplished this thing.

00:15:16.780 --> 00:15:19.600
Our clipper ships are taking off on schedules for all parts of the world.

00:15:20.140 --> 00:15:23.320
I'm glad of that, Mr. Burns, because I'll need some fast-paced provisions, Dr. Washington.

00:15:23.850 --> 00:15:25.330
Government has a new job waiting for me.

00:15:25.930 --> 00:15:27.710
There's just one more favor you can do me, eh?

00:15:27.990 --> 00:15:28.410
Name it.

00:15:29.200 --> 00:15:29.980
Take Billy back with me.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:32.780
to America, by the time he returns to school, I'll be glad to.

00:15:33.310 --> 00:15:38.410
Gee, that's swell, I guess you know Peggy's going back to America too.

00:15:38.960 --> 00:15:40.960
Wouldn't it be swell if we all went back together?

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:43.620
I don't think there'll be any doubt about that time.

00:15:48.280 --> 00:15:48.680
Jerry!

00:16:07.630 --> 00:16:09.410
When did you join the circus?

00:16:09.860 --> 00:16:12.100
Oh, you mean the uniform. Pretty swell, huh?

00:16:12.780 --> 00:16:15.560
Well, you see, Dr. Treanor is forming a company

00:16:15.560 --> 00:16:16.960
to dig the jade out of the mountain,

00:16:17.020 --> 00:16:19.740
and I'm chief pilot, charge of transportation.

00:16:20.140 --> 00:16:21.020
We're fine, Jerry.

00:16:22.060 --> 00:16:25.920
Sure, boy, I guess if uniforms have anything to do with it,

00:16:25.920 --> 00:16:27.380
I'll be a greater pilot than Lindbergh.

00:17:04.950 --> 00:17:08.510
Give me a motor's roar, give me a plane to soar.

00:17:11.160 --> 00:17:12.140
Thank you.

00:17:13.050 --> 00:17:13.630
Be a thrill.

00:17:17.430 --> 00:17:17.970
Thank you.
